    "privacy_policy_body":
        "Last updated: October 30, 2026\n\nGuest use\nReminders and completion history are stored on your device. Guest records are not automatically uploaded. Firebase may create a user ID for an anonymous session.\n\nAccounts and sync\nWhen you sign in with Google or email, your reminders, notes, tags and completion history are stored under your account in Firebase Cloud Firestore. Firebase Authentication processes your name, email address and account ID. The profile photo supplied by Google is displayed; a photo and name you choose are stored in your private profile. This data is used to provide your account and the app's features.\n\nRetention and deletion\nAn account-specific copy is kept on your device for offline use. Signing out does not delete your account or cloud records. Profile > Delete account removes your reminders, history, profile and sign-in account. A deletion marker without reminder or profile content is retained to prevent other devices from restoring deleted data. Guest records are unaffected. Exported backup files must be deleted separately.\n\nService providers\nGoogle Firebase provides authentication and cloud storage; the Firestore database is in Frankfurt. The app contains no advertising or usage analytics. Notifications are scheduled on your device. Photo access is used only for the profile image you select.\n\nContact and deletion requests\nContact emrealidemirel@gmail.com for privacy or account deletion requests. Do not share your password; verification of account ownership may be required.",
